   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Common verbs with «essere»",
     "texto": [
      "Many common verbs of movement or change form the passato prossimo with **essere**: **andare** → andato, **venire** → venuto, **arrivare** → arrivato, **partire** → partito, **uscire** (to go out) → uscito, **tornare** (to return) → tornato, **rimanere** (to stay) → **rimasto**. Just because a verb indicates movement doesn't tell you which auxiliary to use: learn which auxiliary each common verb takes.",
      "All reflexive verbs form this tense with **essere**: **Mi sono alzato** (I got up)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Agreement",
     "texto": [
      "With «essere», the past participle agrees with the subject, like an adjective: **andato** (he), **andata** (she), **andati** (they, masculine), **andate** (they, feminine).",
      "A woman says **Sono andata**; two women, **Siamo andate**. In Italian, **you can actually hear this** when speaking."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
